<title>BELGIUM: BARCO STRENGTHENS POSITION IN INSPECTION SYSTEMS.</title>
<headline>BARCO STRENGTHENS POSITION IN INSPECTION SYSTEMS.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian electronics group Barco NV said on Tuesday it agreed with Advanced Machine Vision Corp of the U.S. to buy AMV's Pulsarr BV of Eindhoven, the Netherlands, for $8.4 million.</p>
<p>Pulsarr specialises in automated visual inspection. Its equipment is used in the production of deep-frozen potato products, shrimps and vegetables in particular.</p>
<p>Barco said Pulsarr was a perfect match for its Elbicon unit whose inspection machines are developed and produced on the basis of laser and X-ray technology. Pulsarr had 1996 turnover of 16.4 million guilders. The profitable company employs 47.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
